    {
      "title": "Confusion Matrix and Core Metrics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Confusion Matrix and Core Metrics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The confusion matrix",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Actual \\ Predicted",
                "Positive",
                "Negative"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Positive**",
                  "{green:TP}",
                  "{red:FN}"
                ],
                [
                  "**Negative**",
                  "{red:FP}",
                  "{green:TN}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "2x2 table of ==actual vs predicted==",
                "{orange:FP} = ==Type I error== (false alarm)",
                "{purple:FN} = ==Type II error== (miss)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Core metrics",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Metric",
                "Formula",
                "Use when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Accuracy==",
                  "(TP+TN)/(TP+TN+FP+FN)",
                  "classes balanced"
                ],
                [
                  "==Precision==",
                  "TP/(TP+FP)",
                  "false alarms costly (spam filter)"
                ],
                [
                  "==Recall== (sensitivity, TPR)",
                  "TP/(TP+FN)",
                  "misses costly (cancer screening)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Accuracy: share of ==all predictions== that are correct",
                "Precision: of predicted positives, how many were right",
                "Recall: of real positives, how many were found"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Worked example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "TP=40, FP=10, FN=20, TN=930",
                "Accuracy = 970/1000 = ==97%==",
                "Precision = 40/50 = ==80%==",
                "Recall = 40/60 = ==66.7%=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "High accuracy can hide misses",
              "text": "97% accuracy, yet 20 of 60 real positives were missed. Check ==recall== too."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "F1 Score and the Threshold Trade-off",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "F1 Score and the Threshold Trade-off",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. F1 and the Threshold",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==F1== = 2PR/(P+R), the **harmonic mean** of precision and recall",
                "It punishes a gap: P=1.0, R=0.1 gives F1 ≈ ==0.18==, not 0.55",
                "Lower the threshold: {blue:recall up}, {red:precision down}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Raise threshold",
                    "sub": "default 0.5",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fewer positives",
                    "sub": "predicted",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Precision up",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Recall down",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. F-beta and Averaging",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "F-beta = (1+β²)PR/(β²P+R)",
                "==β=2== weights **recall** more",
                "==β=0.5== weights **precision** more"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Average",
                "How"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Macro**",
                  "Classes count equally"
                ],
                [
                  "**Micro**",
                  "Pools all counts; = accuracy for single-label multiclass"
                ],
                [
                  "**Weighted**",
                  "Averages by class support"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. In sklearn",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from sklearn import metrics as m",
                "m.precision_recall_fscore_support(y_true, y_pred)",
                "m.classification_report(y_true, y_pred)"
              ],
              "note": "both report P, R, F1 and support per class"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "F1 ignores TN, so ==state the threshold== with any F1 you report."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ROC Curve and AUC",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ROC Curve and AUC",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The ROC Curve",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ROC== plots {green:TPR} (y) against {red:FPR} = FP/(FP+TN) (x)",
                "The threshold sweeps from ==1 to 0==, tracing one point per cutoff"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reading AUC",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "AUC",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1.0",
                  "**perfect** ranking"
                ],
                [
                  "0.5",
                  "random guessing (the diagonal)"
                ],
                [
                  "below 0.5",
                  "labels are **inverted**"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==AUC== = area under the ROC curve",
                "= P(random positive is scored above a random negative)",
                "{green:Threshold-independent}: measures ranking only",
                "Says nothing about ==calibration== or the best cutoff"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Imbalance and sklearn",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Huge ==TN== count keeps FPR tiny, so ROC/AUC looks **optimistic**",
                "On heavy imbalance use the precision-recall curve and ==PR-AUC== (average precision)"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, average_precision_score",
                "roc_auc_score(y_true, y_score)",
                "average_precision_score(y_true, y_score)"
              ],
              "note": "y_score = probabilities or scores"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Scores, not labels",
              "text": "`roc_auc_score` needs ==probabilities or scores==. Hard 0/1 labels collapse the curve to one point."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Regression Metrics: MAE, RMSE, R2",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Regression Metrics: MAE, RMSE, R2",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Error Metrics",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Metric",
                "Formula",
                "Notes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==MAE==",
                  "`mean(|y−ŷ|)`",
                  "target's own units; robust to outliers"
                ],
                [
                  "MSE",
                  "`mean((y−ŷ)²)`",
                  "squared units; squaring punishes big errors"
                ],
                [
                  "==RMSE==",
                  "`√MSE`",
                  "own units; RMSE ≥ MAE; big gap = outliers"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. R² Score",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "R² = 1 − ==SS_res/SS_tot==: share of variance explained",
                "R² = 0: same as predicting the ==mean==",
                "{red:Negative} on test data: worse than the mean",
                "Extra features never lower ==training R²==",
                "Use ==adjusted R²== to penalize useless features"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choosing One",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pick",
                "When"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==MAE==",
                  "all errors cost the same"
                ],
                [
                  "==RMSE==",
                  "big misses are disproportionately bad"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Example: y=[3,5,7], ŷ=[2,5,10] gives errors −1, 0, +3"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "y = [3, 5, 7]; p = [2, 5, 10]",
                "e = [a - b for a, b in zip(y, p)]",
                "mae = sum(map(abs, e)) / 3",
                "rmse = (sum(x * x for x in e) / 3) ** .5",
                "print(round(mae, 2), round(rmse, 2))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1.33 1.83"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Read the gap",
              "text": "RMSE well above MAE means a few ==large misses==. R² can go **negative** on test data."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Class Imbalance and How to Handle It",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Class Imbalance and How to Handle It",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Accuracy Fails",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Always predict majority: ==99% accuracy== on 1% positives, zero recall",
                "Judge with {green:recall}, precision, F1 and ==PR-AUC==",
                "Stratified splits keep the class ratio in every fold"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Fixes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fix",
                "How",
                "Data changed?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Stratify",
                  "`train_test_split(..., stratify=y)`, `StratifiedKFold`",
                  "No"
                ],
                [
                  "Class weights",
                  "`class_weight='balanced'`, XGBoost `scale_pos_weight`",
                  "No"
                ],
                [
                  "Resample",
                  "Over, under, or ==SMOTE== (interpolates new minority points)",
                  "Train only"
                ],
                [
                  "Threshold",
                  "Tune on validation set, not 0.5; cheapest fix",
                  "No"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Leakage",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Resampling before the split leaks synthetic copies into test",
                "Scores get inflated",
                "Resample inside the CV pipeline"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from imblearn.pipeline import Pipeline",
                "from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE",
                "pipe = Pipeline([(\"smote\", SMOTE()), (\"clf\", clf)])",
                "cross_val_score(pipe, X, y, cv=StratifiedKFold(5),",
                "                scoring=\"average_precision\")"
              ],
              "note": "SMOTE refits on each training fold only"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Order matters",
              "text": "Split first, ==resample train only==, score on the untouched test set."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Metrics Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Metrics Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Classification Formulas",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Metric",
                "Formula"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Accuracy",
                  "`(TP+TN)/N`"
                ],
                [
                  "Precision",
                  "`TP/(TP+FP)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Recall",
                  "`TP/(TP+FN)`"
                ],
                [
                  "F1",
                  "`2PR/(P+R)`"
                ],
                [
                  "FPR",
                  "`FP/(FP+TN)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pick the Metric",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "False alarms hurt",
                  "==Precision=="
                ],
                [
                  "Misses hurt",
                  "==Recall=="
                ],
                [
                  "Need balance",
                  "==F1=="
                ],
                [
                  "Ranking quality",
                  "==AUC=="
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Imbalanced data: ==ignore accuracy==, use ==PR-AUC== or F1",
                "Stratify splits, use class weights, **tune the threshold**"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:MAE}: typical error",
                "{orange:RMSE}: punishes outliers",
                "{purple:R²}: variance explained, can be **negative**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Never Do",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Resample before splitting",
                "Feed hard labels to `roc_auc_score`",
                "Skip reporting the threshold used"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Resample only the training data, give AUC ==scores==, and always state the **threshold**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
